        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add queued webhook support",
        "body": "Related: #100939\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nHigh-volume webhook producers can call OpenClaw thousands of times in a burst, but the current webhook path immediately schedules work without durable backlog visibility or queue-level parallelism controls.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds configured webhook queues under hooks.queues, a durable SQLite hook_queue_items store, queue-backed HTTP ingestion at POST /hooks/queue/{id}, per-queue parallelism, default isolated session execution, and shared hook agent dispatch between immediate and queued webhook paths.\n\nIt also exposes hooks.queues and hooks.queue.items over Gateway RPC and adds Control UI queue summaries, status counts, and recent item inspection in the Automation/Cron page.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can enqueue bursty webhook work, inspect queue depth and queued/running/completed/error items, and tune concurrency without overwhelming the application. Existing immediate webhook endpoints remain available.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/hook-queue-store.test.ts src/gateway/hooks.test.ts src/gateway/server.hooks.test.ts ui/src/lib/cron/index.test.ts ui/src/pages/cron/view.test.ts - passed, 172 gateway tests and 65 UI tests\n- node scripts/format-docs.mjs --check - passed\n- node scripts/check-docs-mdx.mjs docs README.md - passed\n- ./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 on touched TS/CSS files - passed\n- git diff --check - passed\n- pnpm build - passed\n- Autoreview follow-up: accepted FIFO finding fixed with sequence ordering and a regression test. A later docs accordion finding was checked against docs/automation/cron-jobs.md lines 397-450 and rejected as a false positive; single-file MDX and docs format checks pass.\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex). Agent transcript logs are not included.",
